## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} {outcomes} />

## The two causes

### `parser`: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports · <a href={tickets.parser}>ticket #1</a>

The shared parser read dates month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so
7 April could be stored as 4 July. Dates with days 1 to 12 can swap day and month. The desk
files day-first tenants' app, email and booking-v2 form reports here, including the one-day
observations below. #1 is closed COMPLETED following the parser fix.

### `hint`: <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports · <a href={tickets.hint}>ticket #2</a>

The booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` but read input in the tenant's day-first order.
These are form reports at booking-v3 tenants; those tenants' app and email reports belong
to parser. #2 is closed NOT_PLANNED because booking-v3 was retired. This is a different
outcome from fixing the hint or parser.

## One-day observations, included in parser

The desk's `desk-notes.json` flags <ProblemCount ticket={4471} observations /> reports whose
bodies describe one-day moves or timing anomalies, listed above.
Their IDs remain in the <ProblemCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> parser reports, counted once. They do not establish a
separate timezone/DST root cause.

[Ticket #3](https://github.com/waustin45/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3) is closed DUPLICATE
of [#1](https://github.com/waustin45/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1), as is the replacement
parser [#4](https://github.com/waustin45/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/4). The engineering
update does not confirm whether the parser fix resolves the one-day observations. Neither
success nor failure of that fix on these observations has been verified.

## How the split is made

- One ID, one report: `uniqueById` removes identical export repeats.
- `groupByCause` in the original `causes.ts` uses tenant locale, form and channel. Intake's
  browser-based tag is a guess; the table keeps it visible for comparison.
- `split.ts` keeps the cause totals separate from overlapping desk-note observations.
- Counts come from the original report export and tenant directory when the page renders.
  Historical timestamps and classification are unchanged.
- Ticket dispositions were checked on 2026-10-28; they and the engineering update are later
  evidence, not fields in the 2026-10-04 export.

## Lessons

- Read the body and the way in before merging. [Proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause)
  and [triage guidance](/kb/triage/dedupe) replace subject-only matching subject to Austin's review.
- Preserve contradictory observations without turning them into a verified cause or counting
  them twice. Keep unknown cases separate for review.

